# ── Database (Supabase Postgres) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The game will not start without a database (README §2–4).
#
# In Supabase: Dashboard → your project → Project Settings → Database →
# Connection string. Copy BOTH strings (replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the
# database password you chose when creating the project):
#
# DATABASE_URL — "Transaction" pooler (port 6543). Used by the running game,
# including on Vercel. Transaction pooling is what lets many short-lived
# serverless instances share Supabase's connection limit.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-YOUR_REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# DIRECT_URL — "Session" pooler (port 5432) or the direct connection
# (db.YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432). Used ONLY by drizzle-kit
# (npm run db:push / db:migrate) to create the tables. Never point
# drizzle-kit at the 6543 transaction pooler.
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-YOUR_REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
#
# Local PostgreSQL instead of Supabase? Both lines can be the same, e.g.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/gacha_debt
#
# Optional: connections per server instance (default 1 — keep it low on
# Vercel + Supabase, see src/db/index.ts).
# DB_POOL_MAX=1

# ── Google sign-in (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty to disable the Google button (email + guest still work).
# Production: in Google Cloud Console add this Authorized redirect URI,
# exactly:  https://YOUR-DEPLOYMENT-DOMAIN/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Public URL of this deployment. On Vercel set this to your production
# domain (no trailing slash), e.g. https://gachadebtgame.vercel.app
# Locally: http://localhost:3000
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Maintenance mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ON by default. While on, the home route serves the maintenance notice (with
# Penelope), /api/game refuses every action with 503, and any tab that is
# already playing gets kicked out within ~15 seconds by the /api/status poll.
#
# Set this to "off" to open the doors again. Anything else - missing, "true",
# "1", "lol" - keeps them shut. See DEPLOYMENT.md §8.
MAINTENANCE_MODE=off
